# The custodians' restart for a new image (D3, 2026-10-06): run by beanpool-vault-restart.path when the API leaves a
# restart request. Root checks the request and the staged image from the pinned custodian keys before it stops
# anything (usr/lib/beanpool-vault/custodian-restart, src/install/install.ts); only then does it stop the API, remove
# what its user left on the state partition, install the image into the other slot and reboot. The vault comes back
# locked; two custodians unlock it. Kernel and C library fixes take effect here.
[Unit]
Description=BeanPool key vault: install a new image two custodians asked for, and restart

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/lib/beanpool-vault/custodian-restart
